{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_00f42cfcc0b379883aaaeecde4e70528988009e3f419d37b2d9b0dcf0bd2396c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=orchestration","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_aa459bf382d0911670f357bb76d154c164602916bd6480398dd73621e8780109"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Agent orchestration is enabled by default: the model can spawn child agents via spawn_agent, send_message, followup_task, wait_agent, list_agents, and interrupt_agent; children run in isolated worktrees, inherit parent model/governance/policy, and can be tool-narrowed with tool_allowlist.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_066e542d2001fc7243fb5864bd33c099e22e6736f4e36f596d3fe680e8dab508","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_a1d4572b1f36568ab128631ea179dba84749c952a5c0b59b58cff80eb33b1c94","slc_b03be6c2da7eaf8e71c840c7242c5d5a2f3718219e53db97297165468e14efe6"],"source_ids":["src_5388956710b25682926147d6be88924f"],"text":"Colours are semantic tokens defined per theme rather than fixed hex values, and the design system names ACCENT_STATUS_MIN_HUE_DISTANCE as its single hardest rule, asserted over built-in themes in tests.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_258d1f7c307c6485d625c5e905f073f8ded7623b61fa492ac3a4ed1acefff646","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_024cf1c79b0a9b629ae47d0668841f004eba8dd4d25f34cd07473ab58132a416","slc_8a7c63f50fdf3a51209d54bbf14d59314cb6693ca66436450e698b84e70addbf"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Configuration is layered from defaults, a user config file, a forge.toml in the working directory, and environment variables, with environment variables overriding file configuration; MCP servers are configured in trusted user config or explicitly managed configuration.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_2bd9adf3c6409ae8bbc9a0427adb94f8964331ed8a290cb59f5fa2717ffc2f3e","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0ab35d95382ecef40e63da674c1b712e185f6d670f45e25858d3a3935de15ec0","slc_3f4ed5b045e0097ac7c9af1a2eaac6e1c72387acaf30a64ad573d736e568c58b","slc_4899b97de1d05fa12c15a279562298ed8102fb02cc234b2494a8a6380fb44eb7"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Forge ships native provider routes for OpenAI, Anthropic, xAI Grok (OAuth), OpenAI Codex subscriptions, OpenCode Go, OpenCode Zen, and local Ollama, configured via API-key environment variables or /connect.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_329d4d587ab06c1de9527723944f91bdebdb923df166e7c19d052cd93396dcb3","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=workflows","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_2938f879d7c21450cc2d69411457257b2ea8423aa1e05be9d38bb63180d85bee","slc_47e1c21413930f5848c462d49945439f80835f35990731fbb9b1b781c3ac7d66","slc_744e22be7b503fbc377eecf3da44ea40e3d00ebb3d96dc3d93af883e5b586410"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Repository development practice: contributors are told to run cargo fmt --check, cargo clippy with -D warnings, and cargo test --workspace before submitting a change, with further guidance in CONTRIBUTING.md.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_36ad4581810a9b3ba367fe9537726bf8263a1b1a873ee7a1830e6ac5b7ed8d6c","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_70cbe7bb2c2b28076f79be44beb5958f21e21d8473964332b7b9aa026cf593ff"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"There is no permission-mode setting: shell commands and file writes run unprompted with the sandbox as the boundary, MCP tools still prompt, and a deny pattern re-prompts even for shell; ACL denies are hard blocks.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_3a49fbf0a2901f77043dfa1125fb220fa55b3e5dde68153e2d4e45de5c5b33cd","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_5bf765a1fc8a34a06ed54bf8af13e770c150ca4c26015391d7a7ba0299072cd0"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"The TUI exposes in-app slash commands such as /connect, /model, /resume, /continue, /fork, /compact, /terminal, /theme, /effort, /thinking, /status, and /quit.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_44790f6e238d6f684721058537202ab184ad2ca2faae0c54a5402860211a23df","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=components","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0d388eb671efbf0de465a16480c9ae61fc627a455d1d07bb51cf46cdd1892a1b","slc_9aac8ac1bb666530345bd880f6356366dc4abbc0c619f839ea514da957bf5fc7"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Forge is a Rust workspace whose main crates include forge-cli (entry point), forge-tui (terminal interface), forge-core (agent loop and session lifecycle), forge-model, forge-connect, forge-tools, and forge-durable (SQLite journals).","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_4c0151c114a9c6cff8e06e509deccdc9d39182f24734c4ffb908c25ee3ef9533","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_186e6c9714b04116fcd9b8f7967d6d1d1fba85609e13fa90aff526b254822d1b"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"The README documents a residual Linux sandbox gap: read-only mounts do not stop Unix socket connections, so sockets under /var or /opt remain reachable despite masking of /run, /tmp, and home trees; tracked in issue #392.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_575f64b10a34fc4f795dc20341257980e7b8276348252b4a6c946d9ca189e831","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=tools-permissions","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_3e3555fb19cad0f98a811c5acc2ba087609ef49b606359f9bda3736639715f05"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Permission rules come from a personal permissions.toml and a workspace .forge/permissions.toml; the repo-committed file's allow entries are ignored while its deny entries are always honored, so a checked-out repo cannot widen its own blast radius.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_59070727be783aac589a7d99229d4f6816f4a4d4b8ddaeaf9f8019347bd29880","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=dependencies","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_6bfd499393fff09b01484f5c4bbd6a972d13774b2189fcef81096c12e104eb0f","slc_a7cfd657cf7a6a55969b698708d0eda83a58a7495966943b1ad54e283a68b06a","slc_ca30cedacef37a681571f0fea873ab3ad8a3918c9aa22db0f92b289b886052dc"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"On Linux the installer installs the sandbox dependencies bubblewrap and socat if missing (supporting apt, dnf, yum, pacman, zypper, apk); macOS needs nothing extra, and building from source requires Git and Rust 1.97.1 or newer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_67640a0e890da21b03556ddc5384e06873f35d807db5ddd49ce0d9cd099f667f","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_46000153ef786d47794c0c3bc0d22ac95e93eb550e98a002fd2ef4feaa6d23c9","slc_47787a8a7b651d9976d07a7da2afdced39d14b9c49efff1d6339aa0234dc27a8","slc_d66a04d215398a344c2cb0d712240109b579797cc5f974fcb5760d311673d5e9"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"A frontend-independent `forge bench` entry point accepts a piped prompt with flags like --workspace, --journal, --model, --route-id, --effort, and --approve-all, emitting one JSON response on stdout and logs on stderr.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8dabe99f628269fcc9df8fd081fbbc9fa831e954d274b63a42a533887f568276","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=limitations","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_61a48b2c28ee687701efa515bab83be6bc9a54b892070c3a4fc016187bbcba57"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"There is no native Windows build; Forge runs under WSL2 using the Linux sandbox, and the PowerShell installer detects WSL2 and points to the Linux installer.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8f1cbf5530a23deda01537e2cedf676823793c19414529ea1dde1db0fdacd123","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=design-choices","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_e1a196263c5b3de892ccb59e5c8674a8b0c0b037225b762ca94a638db877ee96"],"source_ids":["src_5388956710b25682926147d6be88924f"],"text":"Core UX invariants include exactly one effective keyboard owner at a time, colour never being the sole state indicator, approvals and failures outranking routine activity, and refusing to render below an enforced minimum of 80x18.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_8f9e074f5905c940945bf1c2385b5fd1eb77dab5fd165bb7fb7c49bf543e6a43","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=specifications","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_fc36db6fe5e4d3135ca3e3e9080bffceae1a227353b6e4cb433f7b150d8087d4"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Forge is an open-source terminal coding environment for working with AI agents, combining agent conversations, file explorer, Vim-style editing, shell, diffs, approvals, and multiple durable sessions in one keyboard-driven TUI.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
{"access":"public","created_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","created_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58","evidence_type":"organizational_statement","extraction_confidence":0.8,"id":"clm_9e3af8244a399c9f3eb7c4ea4dbfed9c3a92356209e70f61777d686269145c48","lineage_status":"original_available","polarity":"affirmed","record_type":"claim","review_state":"mechanically_checked","schema_version":"1.0","scope":{"instrument_status":null,"jurisdiction":null,"method":"documented","population":null,"qualifiers":"kind=observation; facet=interfaces","setting":"norvialabs/forge@8a1c5e85ec5c snapshot d8ce37fcadf8e938","timeframe":null},"slice_ids":["slc_0b4a747d9cf7ab7b5db45963e9daeb8bbf02caffb6359b9b4ad9e6247a9e962c","slc_3430d711f0af2f7eea30c17d198cceeeca8223fdc82b6d2c23a6981d4119c96a","slc_348465bf555a2522918413ae0211fdcc921e3a460998851ca90ae93c1ca1858e","slc_507a985f90ca0e2f430ad19d7808c657d037acbfd209d6002d0f65558e05eb32","slc_aa7023497da0a5dc04a8bf7e45a71a3c7cc8c1e5f4bada3cdcf5b3314bb2f17f","slc_b155f6e7d342985ab3e90f1893ffdcef4ddde55b655fd7c0bf92f46ba29153f0","slc_fdb25bf2c0b706042809b7f108554962c19b269c2cd9e0cb8c7df4550d01e854"],"source_ids":["src_baf994dcafae5fa59ab3a0c74139341e"],"text":"Documented CLI forms include bare `forge`, `forge --continue`, `forge --resume [<session-id>]`, and `forge --fork <session-id>`; the default workspace is the current directory, overridable via FORGE_WORKSPACE.","updated_at":"2026-09-14T02:23:41Z","updated_by_operation":"op_697dce27368a4a3299f1a3a4c5e3fa58"}
